<title>USA: Marathon cuts U.S. posted crude oil prices 75 cts.</title>
<headline>Marathon cuts U.S. posted crude oil prices 75 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 75 cents a barrel, effective Wednesday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $17.75 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $15.90 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $17.50 and Oklahoma sweet is $17.75.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
